This folder contains unit tests for Simu5G classes that can be exercised
without a running simulation.

Each *.test file is an opp_test test case: its %activity section becomes the
body of a cSimpleModule::activity() in a one-module network, so the code has a
cComponent to draw random numbers from and can call into libsimu5g directly.

Running the tests
-----------------

    ./runtest                # all tests, against the release library
    ./runtest Foo.test ...   # selected tests
    MODE=debug ./runtest     # against the debug library

or, from the project root,

    make unittests
    make MODE=debug unittests

Both the Simu5G and the INET shared library must be built in the requested
mode, and SIMU5G_ROOT and INET_ROOT must be set (source the setenv script of
both projects). Generated sources, the test executable and the captured
output of each run end up in ./work, which is not under version control.

Writing tests
-------------

Every test is compiled into one shared executable, so anything a test defines
at file scope must either be inline or live inside the test's own %global
section, which opp_test places in a per-test C++ namespace.

lib/ holds header-only helpers shared by several tests; it is on the include
path of every test, but it is not a compiled library and must stay
header-only.

The expected values of the path-loss tests are not recorded from the model:
pathloss_reference.py transcribes the 3GPP formulas independently and prints
every value the tests use, grouped by test file. Run it to re-derive them, or
to work out the value of a new case; the formula belongs in a comment next to
the check it justifies.

Expected failures
-----------------

A few tests carry an %expected-failure directive. Those record a defect that
has been identified but not yet fixed: they assert what the model ought to
produce, and are reported as EXPECTEDFAIL rather than FAIL until it does. The
%description of each explains the deviation. When one is fixed, drop the
%expected-failure line and fold the checks back into the main test file it
was split out of.
